  "id": "Compound::DB00227 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Lovastatin exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with all three paths showing that Cyp2c19 participates in the same type of enzymatic activity—limonene monooxygenase activity—regardless of the specific isoform (Cyp2c19 vs. Cyp2c19). The shared participation in this activity by Cyp2c9 suggests a potential mechanistic link between Lovastatin and Cyp2c9, as it is likely that Lovastatin inhibits the activity of Cyp2c9 through the same pathway. The high scores from the paths indicate a strong and consistent relationship, supported by the shared functional role of Cyp2c19 in the enzymatic process. The evidence suggests that Lovastatin may act as a competitive inhibitor of Cyp2c9, thereby affecting its ability to metabolize substrates. The integration of these paths highlights a robust, mechanistically sound relationship between Lovastatin and Cyp2c9, grounded in the shared enzymatic function of Cyp2c19.",
